    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyrĭeus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ei,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑριεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a poor
				Bœotian</i>, <i>father of Orion</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. F.
				5, 499</span></i>; <i><span class="en">535</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyrĭēŭs</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrisyl.</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyrĭēa proles,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Orion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 719</span></i>
			.</div>
